# OpenContrib Engine Rules for Cursor

When working on open-source contributions or triaging issues:
1. Verify environment & capabilities: `opencontrib doctor` and `opencontrib capability list`.
2. Inspect findings via Smart Pointers: `opencontrib pointer list` and `opencontrib pointer resolve <uri> --view slice`.
3. Isolate workspace in a clean Git worktree: `opencontrib workspace prepare --repo <owner/repo> --issue <id>`.
4. Establish empirical reproduction (RED→GREEN): capture the failing baseline with `opencontrib evidence capture-red --test-cmd "<test_cmd>" --assertion "<pattern>"`, apply the fix, then verify with `opencontrib evidence verify-green --test-cmd "<test_cmd>"`.
5. Pre-flight governance audit: `opencontrib governance audit --patch <file> --pr-title "<title>"`.
6. Draft PR following repo standards: `opencontrib governance pr-template --issue <id> --issue-title "<title>" --summary "<summary>"`.
7. Synchronize contribution flywheel: `opencontrib flywheel sync --repo <owner/repo>`.
